# [Minimum Score by Changing Two Elements](https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-score-by-changing-two-elements/)

### Approach: Sorting

- Sort the array in ascending order.
- We can change at most two elements, so we have three possible cases:
  1. Change the two smallest elements.
  2. Change the two largest elements.
  3. Change the smallest and largest elements.
- Calculate the difference between the maximum and minimum remaining elements for all three cases.
- Return the minimum of these three differences.

### Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int minimizeSum(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        int n = nums.size();

        int ans1 = abs(nums[2] - nums[n-1]);
        int ans2 = abs(nums[n-3] - nums[0]);
        int ans3 = abs(nums[1] - nums[n-2]);

        return min({ans1, ans2, ans3});
    }
};
```

### Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n log n) – Sorting the array.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) – Constant auxiliary space (excluding sorting overhead).
